Yes, Istio is automatically injecting a sidecar (istio-proxy) into the Datadog agent pod, and that is causing the startup probe failure.

Since Datadog does not need Istio’s sidecar, it is best to disable automatic sidecar injection for Datadog pods.

✅ Why Is This Happening?
Your namespace (default) has Istio auto-injection enabled (istio-injection=enabled).
This means Istio injects the sidecar into all pods in the namespace, including the Datadog agent pod.
But Datadog doesn’t need an Istio proxy, and this is causing failures in the istio-proxy container.
✅ How to Disable Istio Sidecar for Datadog Pods
You have two options:

🔹 Option 1: Disable Istio Injection for Datadog Only
You can disable Istio sidecar injection for Datadog pods without affecting other services.

1️⃣ Patch the Datadog agent DaemonSet to exclude Istio injection:

bash
Copy
Edit
kubectl annotate daemonset datadog-agent -n default sidecar.istio.io/inject="false"
2️⃣ Restart Datadog agent to apply changes:

bash
Copy
Edit
kubectl rollout restart daemonset datadog-agent -n default
🔹 Option 2: Disable Istio Injection for the Entire default Namespace
If only Datadog is running in default, you can disable Istio sidecar injection for all pods in default:

bash
Copy
Edit
kubectl label namespace default istio-injection=disabled --overwrite
Then restart Datadog:

bash
Copy
Edit
kubectl rollout restart daemonset datadog-agent -n default
✅ Verify That Datadog is Running Without Istio Sidecar
After disabling injection, check if Datadog is running without an Istio proxy:

bash
Copy
Edit
kubectl get pods -A --selector=sidecar.istio.io/injected=true
If Datadog is still listed, the sidecar is still being injected.

To check Datadog pods:

bash
Copy
Edit
kubectl get pods -n default | grep datadog
kubectl describe pod <datadog-agent-pod-name> -n default
Confirm that istio-proxy is not running inside the Datadog pod.

💡 Summary
Istio is automatically injecting a sidecar into Datadog, causing failures.
Solution: Disable Istio injection for Datadog pods using:
bash
